  <content>
  <section><title>Activity</title>
<para>The function \(B\) is defined by the equation \(B(x) = 10x + 25\). Use the graphing tool here or technology outside the course. Graph the function.</para>
<div class="os-raise-ib-desmos-gc" data-schema-version="1.0"/>
<para>If needed, remember -</para>
<list>
  <item>You can collapse the equation entry tab by selecting the button.</item>
  <item>To change the scale along either the x- or \(y\)-axis, click on the wrench button and then enter minimum and maximum values for each axis and set the step value.</item>
  <item>To find a point on the line, click on the line and drag the mouse along the line to display the ordered pairs for each location.</item>
</list>
<!--Question 1 -->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para>What is the value of \(B(6)\)?</para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para>\(B(6) = 85\)</para>
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Question 2 -->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para>What were the window values you used for the \(x\)-axis? (Write the values as an inequality.)</para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para>\(-1 \leq x \leq 7\)</para>
  </solution></exercise>
